\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Captum Integrated-Gradients attribution on held-out malaria cells (CNN, black baseline, 32 steps). Left: input; middle: attribution; right: overlay. On Parasitized cells the attribution hotspots coincide with the visible parasite bodies (often at the cell periphery); on Uninfected cells attribution is diffuse. Quantified in \texttt  {results/malaria/saliency\_ig.json}.}}{27}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Pneumonia confident joint from the 3-fold out-of-fold census. The off-diagonal mass is again strongly one-directional: 973 training images labelled \emph  {pneumonia} cross-validate as \emph  {normal}, vs 23 in the opposite direction.}}{28}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Out-of-fold confidence by true label (seaborn KDE). The one-directional label-noise mass is visible as the heavy wrong-side tails: Parasitized-labelled cells with near-zero parasite confidence, and PNEUMONIA-labelled films with near-zero pneumonia confidence.}}{29}{}\protected@file@percent }
